# Cargo build output.
target/
# platform-api is only ever consumed as a path dependency -- by platform-pyo3
# beside it and by the daemons' own workspace -- so nothing ever resolves
# against a lock file of its own.  One appears anyway the moment somebody runs
# cargo inside this directory, and then sits in `git status` looking like it
# belongs to the crate.  platform-pyo3 keeps its lock because check.sh builds
# that one standalone.
Cargo.lock
